Q.energy_security += 3;
Q.market_liberal_support += 2;
Q.economic_issue_salience += 1;
Q.razem_dissent += 4;
Q.labor_dissent += 3;
Q.workers_support -= 2;
Q.last_policy_stage = "Institutional decision";
Q.last_policy_authority = "Regulatory approval and private investment decisions";
Q.last_policy_implementation = "Small modular reactor fleet licensed on industrial sites";
Q.news_headline = "Poland licenses a private small-reactor fleet for industrial heat and power";
!}

The regulator gets resources, the licensing path is written, and the first units
are sited beside chemical plants and district-heating systems that currently burn
coal. It is genuinely the fastest decarbonisation available, and almost none of
it belongs to the public.

Konin gets nothing from this decision, which is the part our own people cannot
forgive. The lignite region watches a fleet of reactors approved for the
industrial customers of large private companies while its own site remains a
letter of intent. Our energy spokesperson defends the emissions arithmetic and
is asked, on air, who will own the electricity.

- @poland_event_queue: License the fleet

